For compound interest:
Let the rate of interest = R% and sum = Rs. P
Then, amount in 5 years;
4525 = P X (1+ R/100)<sup>5</sup>
And, amount in 6 years;
5430 = P X (1+R/100)<sup>6</sup>
Now, 4525/5430 = 1/(1+R/100)
R=20
Therefore, SI on Rs.6400 at 20% rate of interest in 7.5 years;
6400 X 20 X 7.5/100= = Rs. 9600

